  <section|<verbatim|local-splitting.tex>><label|local-splittingtex>

  Inspected full source: <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/LOCAL_SPLITTING/{Projection,Atoms,Raw,Recovery,Merge,Funding}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/FOUNDATIONS/{Readout,TestBounds,LinkBounds,Split,Regular,Primary}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Planned/ATOM_GUARDED_LAYOUT/{Assembly,Guards}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/{Chalet,Wallet,Visit,Coffer,Cloudlet,Orchestra,Flavor}.lean>.
  Inspected meaning-determining excerpts: <verbatim|RG/Masks>
  BudgetPoint/Regular/supBounds; <verbatim|Next/FOUNDATIONS/JetReads>
  JetTest/Reads/unique; <verbatim|Lattice/Support> Nonwrapping;
  <verbatim|Work/G02> endpointGerm and linkGerm.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Jet existence and wrapping convention:
    <verbatim|YM.Next.Foundations.read_projection>,
    <verbatim|YM.Next.Foundations.exists_read>,
    <verbatim|YM.Push.Local.project_reads>.

    <item>Uniform logarithmic link estimate and fixed-order tensor/readout
    bound: <verbatim|YM.Next.Foundations.testLog_bound>,
    <verbatim|test_bound>, <verbatim|price_of_readout>. Text follows compact
    normalized profile argument, not a claimed uniform analyticity radius.
    Real Volterra resolvent is <verbatim|YM.Work.G02.endpointGerm>.

    <item>Exact mask correction: <verbatim|YM.Push.Local.convert_atom>,
    <verbatim|charge_atom>.

    <item>Exact pointed product bijection:
    <verbatim|YM.Push.Local.Slots.recover> in Recovery. The text gives both
    maps and the absolute-summability qualification.

    <item>Price: <verbatim|YM.Push.Local.packBudget>,
    <verbatim|Slots.forceCost>, <verbatim|price_meeting>,
    <verbatim|price_join>, <verbatim|income_of_reserved>.

    <item>Built coefficient/density: <verbatim|YM.Push.Local.Raw.build>,
    <verbatim|build_density>, <verbatim|build_remBound>; actual
    guaranteed-address version is <verbatim|YM.Planned.GuardedAtom.Guard.mint>,
    <verbatim|usage>, <verbatim|value_mint>, <verbatim|tab_mint>. Prose uses
    original predicates with guaranteed eligibility directly; temporary
    proof-only predicate erasure is suppressed as scaffolding.

    <item>Grouped response and profile: <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.coda>,
    <verbatim|vigor>, <verbatim|budgetProfile>.
  </itemize-minus>

  Independent reviewer found three precision defects in first draft:
  undefined nonwrapping convention, unqualified summation of merge costs, and
  literal <verbatim|qquad>/<verbatim|quad> text from missing LaTeX
  backslashes. All repaired in hash <verbatim|de7802139e0416e3ebe5ba6f607fd8b7cea56ee3261e86005b959a5f22119c6f>;
  independent reviewer confirmed the local mathematical/source pass. Raw
  one-step expansion remains a separate producer obligation; this chapter
  does not discharge it.

  <section|<verbatim|local-sections.tex>><label|local-sectionstex>

  Inspected full <verbatim|Lean/YM/Work/{G01,G03,G04,G05,G06,G07}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Work/G05/Pose>, <verbatim|Work/G06/{Formula,Pose}>,
  <verbatim|Work/G07/Stencil>, <verbatim|Bid/Source>. Inspected
  <verbatim|Source/Drops> finite radial spaces, sampler, Vision and insight;
  <verbatim|Work/G06/Average> through the covariance proof;
  <verbatim|Maxwell/Exterior> located radial contraction identity. The proof
  of that identity is written explicitly from Euler's identity and radial
  gauge, not assumed from the name.

  Main chain: <verbatim|YM.Work.G03.answer> (all plaquette linearizations
  separate via shrinking-grid highest-degree argument, then finite kernel
  descent), <verbatim|YM.Work.G04.answer> (equivariant orthogonal splitting),
  <verbatim|YM.Source.Drops.insight> (analytic recovery),
  <verbatim|YM.Work.G05.answer> (shared Taylor recovery and lower slot
  degree), <verbatim|YM.Work.G06.answer> (finite signed averaging and actual
  matrix-entry polynomial realization), <verbatim|YM.Work.G07.answer>
  (fixed-stencil derivative and threshold powers),
  <verbatim|YM.Next.Foundations.priced> and <verbatim|stencil_price> (finite
  price table/room). Initial hash <verbatim|ba31f8b09439e162ba5207c4125ec0909fa4da18518f52993e4fc05191b2804f>
  is under independent review. Does not prove calendar affordability.

  <section|Search and validation><label|search-and-validation>

  Shared literature README consulted. This is an explicit source-specific
  finite construction, with standard finite-dimensional Taylor calculus, the
  analytic inverse function theorem and elementary operator power series; no
  extensive external literature search was undertaken. No claim of novelty.

  Commands actually run: targeted <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|cat>,
  <verbatim|sed> reads above; one attempted read of nonexistent
  <verbatim|Push/LOCAL_SPLITTING/Reserves.lean> failed and was replaced by
  the actual Merge/Funding/Guards files. No Lean source edits or new Lean
  build. The 157-page integrated PDF was built before the final precision
  fixes and local-sections insertion. Five contact sheets covering pages
  18\U32 and 108\U133 were viewed. Literal qquad/quad text in the old
  local-splitting render was visible and has been repaired; corrected render
  remains pending. No other clipping or layout issue was identified in this
  overview inspection.

  Local-sections wording clarified explicit signed covariance and reversed
  ordered link derivative list, yielding hash
  <verbatim|a9987194194cc332b06e0b4d58e7420ff33169663e10914ec80fe41f096397ac>;
  reviewer notified. Kernel reflows preserve mathematical passes at hashes
  <verbatim|4e831e4a8fc153705abdf4a6ca47668873393bf134ec92c79583be836546e7e3>
  and <verbatim|2a20c8dc96e80d552370b98a23457efa1cd165c430f714f6e4ddfbb5d81ade98>.

  <section|Final local section and elementary transfer
  snapshots><label|final-local-section-and-elementary-transfer-snapshots>

  Independent reviewer confirmed local-sections hash
  <verbatim|a9987194194cc332b06e0b4d58e7420ff33169663e10914ec80fe41f096397ac>.
  <verbatim|leaf-transfer.tex> hash <verbatim|e7234ac0f3ce52aa92ebcd456ccaadfbce2f4f4c63ce2f423211cb5a311ad62a>
  passed local mathematical/source review after two fixes: positive
  square-root forced allowance is explicit, and the transferred singleton
  profile is a separate hypothesis beside the scalar raw density identity.
  Sources inspected: <verbatim|MergeProof/Blush/{Parcel,Wind,Confetti,Ribbon}.lean>,
